{
  "artifact": "mindmake-approved-production-routes-r46",
  "recordedAt": "2026-09-25",
  "status": "candidate record. The leadership chapters' benefit headlines stay inside their stage on a phone, and the practice scenes build with scroll on a phone.",
  "scopeRequested": "Krish, 2026-09-25, with two phone screenshots of the homepage: \"Two other issues: 1. The CRO screenshot shows text flying off the right-hand side of the page. 2. In the other screenshot there is a vertically stacked section which should really build with scroll, with that left-to-right green line animation. Or if you can think of anything more surprising and delightful than that, I'm all ears for a bit of variety.\" The plan proposing the signal sweep was approved before implementation.",
  "sessionDecisions": [
    "The benefits stage (shared by / and /new-age-leadership) stacks all six statements in one grid cell whose auto column grew to the widest phrase any statement could not break. keepLastWords held \"forgotten observation.\" together (385px at 412), so every statement laid out about 15px wider than the stage that hides its overflow and lost the ends of its lines. The column is now minmax(0, 1fr), the phone column of .human-proof likewise, and the phone headline is clamp(34px, 10.5vw, 58px) (short phones min(clamp(32px, 7vh, 44px), 10.5vw)), at which the longest kept pair fits the measure from 320px. Made in the hand-written R6 layer; new-age-leadership-r5.css is regenerated from it.",
    "keepLastWords' clip test returned early whenever a block did not overflow its own box, so a heading that grew its track past a clipping ancestor kept its join. It now also takes back a join when the block is wider than an ancestor that hides its overflow; scrolling ancestors are excluded, so a card waiting off screen in a carousel keeps its joins.",
    "qa:line-breaks gains a clipped-text rule: a word past the edge of an ancestor that hides its overflow, or past the viewport, fails; a scroller's overflow does not. Its negative control carries a clipped line that must be reported and a scroller that must not. Against the pre-fix build it reports the benefits 8px past the stage at 390x844; after the fix it reports nothing on 31 routes.",
    "On a phone at least 480px tall the practice introduction still scrolls, then the scenes pin as one frame under the masthead and build by the signal sweep: a 1px mint line crosses the frame left to right, uncovering the next scene behind it (a scroll-scrubbed clip-path), while the outgoing words leave and the incoming ones settle once it has passed. The stage buttons become a rail at the frame's foot in the reach chapter's language, a hairline with a 2px mint fill that travels from stop to stop with the sweep; each stop is a 44px button that scrolls to its scene. The progress is read from layout offsets, not innerHeight, and is scrubbed both ways.",
    "Reduced motion keeps the pin and changes scenes at the same points without a sweep. A phone held sideways (under 480px tall) and a page without scripts keep the scenes one after another; in that flow no visible scene carries aria-hidden. On the homepage, where the chapters own film playback, only the scene on screen and the one being uncovered play; /new-age-leadership keeps its own playback and motion toggle.",
    "Desktop (over 900px) is unchanged. The homepage scroll contract now declares the phone practice case; the browser check asserts the phone pin, the rail's 44px stops and the last stop filling the rail, and that 720x450 keeps the stacked flow. The new-age production check needs no change: its sweep reads the active scene once the scenes are stacked in one cell, and its negative control, run at 1440, still removes the desktop pin. STATE.md's non-regression item and 03_DESIGN_CONTRACT.md record the new phone behaviour."
  ],
